  "releaseNotes": "0.1.3 — The user data stream's listenKey is now registered as a known secret on the named client's masker the moment it is obtained, on both the create (POST) and the renewal (PUT), so it is replaced with the mask segment wherever it later appears — including places a field-name rule cannot reach, such as a path segment of an address or a message another package has already formatted. A renewal that hands back a different key registers that one too, and the earlier key is deliberately left registered: masking a lapsed credential once more costs nothing, masking it once less is a leak. BinanceUserDataFeed gains a constructor overload taking an Ozakboy.Security SecretMasker (obtain it with provider.GetOzakboyHttpMasker(BinanceConstants.HttpClientName)); the existing overload is unchanged and registers nothing, and AddBinanceUserData now supplies the masker automatically. Ozakboy.Security 0.1.1 is referenced directly, since the type is now part of the public API. Full notes: https://github.com/ozakboy/Ozakboy.TradeKit.Binance/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
